 107: 
 108: **Abstract, after the damped scalar-charge sentence:**
 109: **Conjectural.** A worked white-dwarf calculation indicates two things about the scalar-driven displacement of the carrier's own matter: it leaves a transient retarded monopole signal with no first-order permanent charge, and it couples to orbital drives only through small static and structural coefficients.
 110: 
 111: **Section 6, after the paragraph on the physical target:**
 112: **Conjectural.** Section 4.6 works through one internal state of the white-dwarf carrier, the scalar-driven displacement of its own matter. That state leaves a transient retarded monopole signal with no first-order permanent charge. Small static and structural coefficients bound its coupling to orbital drives, so it cannot supply a lag at the Section 5 sensitivity. Other internal states of the white dwarfs, and the neutron-star charge of Section 4.3, remain open.
