  19: The drive is an ingoing pulse \(\Psi_{\rm in}=\eta R_d\,\mathcal P((t+x/c)/t_p)\), where \(\mathcal P(s)=(4s(1-s))^4\) on \(0<s<1\) and zero otherwise, with \(t_p=1.717\) ms, \(\eta=10^{-30}\) and \(R_d=6.91\times10^9\) cm. It drives the coupled evolution of baryons, gas, photon transport and one returned GR metric until \(t_e=2t_p\).
  20: 
  21: The readout is \(q=-\Psi_{\rm out}/m_i\) at \(R_d\), the change of \(a_i\) seen in the exterior monopole. It excludes the instantaneous polarization \(\beta_sT_0\delta\varphi\), which belongs to the wave operator; in the coupled calculation that polarization produces a Born scattering of \(1.7\times10^{-10}\) of the incident field. The pulse length \(ct_p\simeq515\) km is far below \(R\), so this is a finite-size response outside the point-particle regime \(\lambda\gg R\).
