 125: q(t)=c_YF(t)+c_\chi\chi(t),\qquad
 126: \beta=\alpha c_\chi,\quad\tau_\chi>0.
 127: \label{eq:model}
 128: \end{equation}
 129: 
 130: The readout may correct a specified observable coupling. Assigning it to a mass or a pairwise gravitational parameter are different modeling choices. Relaxation presupposes an effective dissipative setting; it is not derived from an isolated conservative one-variable action.
