 152: On \(|\omega\tau_\chi|\le\rho<1\), the error is at most \(|\beta|\rho^{N+1}\). Zero lag gives the settled readout \((c_Y+\beta)F\). Zero frequency gives a settled constant shift, but does not eliminate a transient. Zero pole strength eliminates the driven-state contribution to the settled q; an independently initialized transient can remain when c_chi is nonzero.
